Error List counts and graph diffs are build checks, not runs. No benchmark row was added: INDEX still ends at row 59 dated 2026-09-27 (`archive/benchmarks/INDEX.md:80`), identical to the count at the last review.

The only product with run evidence remains the display-loop VI `D1_s1_disp_20260927_041648.vi`: lost frames 3,359 and 5,860 for the original copy versus 16 and 12 for the new VI at 15 beads, 120 s, 90 Hz (`tools/bench/disp_110_abba.json:19-47`), with X/Y/Z bit-identical on replay (INDEX row 59). It was accepted in cycle 110, before the last review. In this window its DELIVERED line was moved out of STATUS into an archive file (`STATUS.md:12`, `archive/2026-10-01-status-cycle123-relocate.md:28`). It sits on the S1 branch, not on the D1 bed chain that every cycle builds on.

The counted output again names `Track_v6_CPU_core_v0.vi` and `Track_v6_CPU_queue_v0.vi` as the deliverables. A search of the whole `2. Tracking` tree finds neither. The counter has reported phantom files for three reviews running.

## 2. Goal alignment

Against the user's numbered list (`project-requirements/parallelization-requirement.md:10-18`) and the project's own goal map:

- **1, split the post-pick loop.** Structural movement only. The ring buffer between loop 1.1 and 1.2 is now at P3a of P2–P6, unrun (`docs/goalmap.json:9`, `STATUS.md:94`).
- **2.1 motor control.** Met in the original (`goalmap.json:15`).
- **2.2 motor reading, the bottleneck the user named.** Not moved since 2026-08-24 (`goalmap.json:21`, status `open`).
- **2.3 camera acquisition in its own loop.** Still `open` (`goalmap.json:27`). The ring work targets it but has not produced a running loop.
- **2.4 scheduler.** Not moved since project start (`goalmap.json:33`).
- **2.5 merge and save.** Loop 1.7 exists on the unrun chain only (`goalmap.json:39`).
- **3, functions run in parallel.** No running VI has more loops than the display-loop VI.
- **Frame loss at load (R4, M10).** No new measurement since row 58 on 09-27. 150 Hz has never been run (`goalmap.json:199-201`).
- **R8, camera settings inside the VI.** The user chose this on 09-25 (`tools/bench/decisions_pending.json:121`). Nothing built, six days later.
- **GPU path (R6).** Open, ranked last by the user.

Unmoved since the project began: motor reading, scheduler, camera acquisition as a running loop, 150 Hz, in-VI frame rate.

